1
00:00:18,440 --> 00:00:21,070
OK, Richard. That's terrific.

2
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:24,970
Your pressure is 120 over 75, and that's fine.

3
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:36,350
Now stand up, please.

4
00:00:36,350 --> 00:00:41,110
Good, it's 122 over 80.

5
00:00:41,110 --> 00:00:45,770
You can sit down now.

6
00:00:45,770 --> 00:00:48,560
When was your last complete physical?

7
00:00:48,560 --> 00:00:49,950
Six months ago.

8
00:00:49,950 --> 00:00:52,180
Good. Do you have any back or knee problems?

9
00:00:52,180 --> 00:00:54,950
Nope. I am in perfect health.

10
00:00:54,950 --> 00:00:56,590
What do you do for a living, Mr. Stewart?

11
00:00:56,590 --> 00:00:57,950
I'm a photographer.

12
00:00:57,950 --> 00:01:00,350
Interesting. What do you photograph?

13
00:01:00,350 --> 00:01:06,020
Everything. The American scene. People, places, events.

14
00:01:06,020 --> 00:01:10,130
Did you ever think of photographing an aerobics class?

15
00:01:10,130 --> 00:01:14,960
No...I can't remember taking pictures of people exercising.

16
00:01:14,960 --> 00:01:16,820
But don't you think it'd be a good subject?

17
00:01:16,820 --> 00:01:20,560
Sure.

18
00:01:20,560 --> 00:01:23,580
I need some good photos for my advertising, Mr. Stewart.

19
00:01:23,580 --> 00:01:25,150
Maybe you can photogragh a class,

20
00:01:25,150 --> 00:01:27,140
and I can give you and Mrs.Stewart

21
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:28,940
a month of classes ree.

22
00:01:28,940 --> 00:01:30,560
When can I photograph a class?

23
00:01:30,560 --> 00:01:32,590
Anytime.

24
00:01:32,590 --> 00:01:33,610
How about today?

25
00:01:33,610 --> 00:01:37,140
Terrific!

26
00:01:37,140 --> 00:01:39,430
Hi.

27
00:01:39,430 --> 00:01:43,730
Oh, hi.

28
00:01:43,730 --> 00:01:44,160
Are we ready to go?

29
00:01:44,160 --> 00:01:44,710
Yeah. Yeah. Let's get in our lines.

30
00:01:44,710 --> 00:01:48,370
We're going to take it slow first.

31
00:01:48,370 --> 00:01:50,260
Stretch up...and we're going to go left first ...

32
00:01:50,260 --> 00:02:03,070
2,3,4 ... now switch. ...

33
00:02:03,070 --> 00:02:04,950
OK, hold to the right.

34
00:02:04,950 --> 00:02:13,320
Sunrises. Stretch it out. Flat back.

35
00:02:13,320 --> 00:02:27,250
Bring it up ... and twists ... and side ... 2, 3 ...

36
00:02:27,250 --> 00:02:35,770
and left ... push ... push ... turn ... hit the floor.

37
00:02:35,770 --> 00:02:50,840
Take it side again .... OK, and switch. Stretch it out.

38
00:02:50,840 --> 00:02:54,160
And we're going to warm down with a tango.

39
00:02:54,160 --> 00:03:11,930
Left, right. Enjoy it.

40
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:14,620
Richard, did you go to the Davis Aerobics class today?

41
00:03:14,620 --> 00:03:20,220
Yes, I went to the aerobics class today.

42
00:03:20,220 --> 00:03:23,190
What is wrong with you?

43
00:03:23,190 --> 00:03:25,790
Nothing. I am in excellent health.

44
00:03:25,790 --> 00:03:29,090
I have ideal blood pressure. A perfect heart.

45
00:03:29,090 --> 00:03:33,950
In other words, I'm in wonderful condition.

46
00:03:33,950 --> 00:03:36,740
Richard, did you go to the aerobics class, really?

47
00:03:36,740 --> 00:03:40,820
And don't forget to invite Susan for dinner.

48
00:03:40,820 --> 00:03:42,480
And your legs don't hurt?

49
00:03:42,480 --> 00:03:46,280
Hurt? What do you mean?

50
00:03:46,280 --> 00:03:50,670
What about your arms? Lift your arms up like this.

51
00:03:50,670 --> 00:03:54,390
And they don't hurt ot even a little?

52
00:03:54,390 --> 00:03:58,700
Nope.

53
00:03:58,700 --> 00:04:01,700
You are in great condition. I can't believe it!
